The OpenBSD result needs a narrower claim: `lca_conf_read()` preserves all-ones after a fault at any offset, but enumeration skips an absent function immediately after its ID-register read. That path never reads its nonzero registers. For the replacement observer, I’ve confirmed that the available Linux binary has both backend symbols; I’m checking that the handler actually calls them and that the assertions would catch bus collapse and the bus-zero alias.
