**VERDICT: Include the bus-zero alias in this round. A single-handler diff can fix it without changing the backend API. My earlier proposal was incomplete; the replacement observer remains unvalidated here.**

**Q1. Reject type-1 bus zero before either backend call.** Keep cycle type separate from the decoded destination bus.

This exact diff targets the current [configuration handler](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_lca.c:89). It passes `git apply --check` from `GXEMUL-SEC/`. It is unapplied and uncompiled; this session has read-only filesystem access.

```diff
--- a/src/devices/dev_lca.c
+++ b/src/devices/dev_lca.c
@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@
